From 07a131e456707d273d62b213783221831d61f54a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: fozzfut <vanolia13@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 21:32:50 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] PartDesign: Body reuses its copy of an unchanged tip (issue
 029)

Body::execute copies the tip shape with the tip's transformation baked
into the geometry (BRepBuilderAPI_Transform with copy) on every
recompute that reaches the Body, also when the tip did not change: a
sketch added to the body, every recompute of a sketch while it is
edited, a second recompute pass. In the GUI the new TShapes then make
the Body's view provider rebuild its whole mesh (31-48 ms Top, 334-431
ms hicmos per recompute).

The copy is a pure function of the tip's shape. It is now memoized per
Body with its complete input (tip TopoDS shape, element map object,
tag, hasher, transformation) and an exact record of the mutable BRep
state of the tip and of the copy (flags, children, tolerances, curve
and point representations, ranges, triangulations; objects by address,
held by handle). The previous copy is handed to Shape.setValue() again
only when the input is equal, the tip's state is unchanged and the copy
is either as it was made (nothing meshed it) or, while the Body is shown
and its placement is unchanged, as the last Shape.setValue() left it.
Otherwise the copy is made as before. Shape.setValue(), the element map
re-tag, notifications and the view provider update run unchanged.

Switch: BaseApp/Preferences/Mod/PartDesign/BodyCopyReuse (default true).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
